  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have to process QQQ queries on a rooted tree. Each node of the tree has a label and a color. Initially, the tree consists of a single node (the root) with label 111 and color c0c_0c0​. There are two types of queries:\n\n\nYou are given an existing node uuu and a color ccc. Let's denote the number of nodes in the tree before this query by kkk. Create a node with label k+1k+1k+1 and color ccc, and add it to the tree as a child of node uuu.\nYou are given a node uuu and a color ccc. For each node with color ccc (possibly including uuu), find its distance from node uuu. The answer to this query is the minimum of these distances, or −1-1−1 if there are no nodes with color ccc in the tree.\nThe input is encoded so that you have to process these queries online.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤Q≤2⋅1051 \\le Q \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤Q≤2⋅105",
      "the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105",
      "ttt is '+' or '?'",
      "uuu is a valid label of a node in the tree",
      "1≤c0,c≤2⋅1051 \\le c_0, c \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤c0​,c≤2⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers QQQ and c0c_0c0​.\nEach of the following QQQ lines contains a character ttt followed by a space and two space-separated integers u′u'u′ and c′c'c′ describing a query.\n\nThe character ttt is '+' for a query of the first type or '?' for a query of the second type.\nLet's denote the answer to the last query of the second type by aaa (a=−1a = -1a=−1 if there have been no queries of the second type so far). The parameters uuu and ccc of the current query can be computed as u=u′⊕(a+1)u = u' \\oplus (a+1)u=u′⊕(a+1) and c=c′⊕(a+1)c = c' \\oplus (a+1)c=c′⊕(a+1).",
    "outputFormat": "For each query of the second type, print a single line containing one integer — the answer to this query.",
    "notes": [],
